From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ash: list and launch NickelOS host Linux apps

NickelOS runs Linux apps (Flatpak, Portage) on the device itself, as
Wayland clients of Exo, instead of in a Crostini VM. nickel-appd
registers them in the GuestOS registry as VM "nickel", container "host",
through the same UpdateApplicationList D-Bus call vm_cicerone uses, and
starts them on request.

- crostini::LaunchCrostiniAppWithIntent() hands apps of VM "nickel" to
  nickel-appd (org.nickelos.Apps.LaunchApplication) before any Crostini
  check; every other launch path would start a VM first.
- crostini::IsNickelNativeAppsAllowed(): the shelf's window tracker
  also runs for host apps (and their publisher, 0012, asks it), which
  need no /dev/kvm and are available in guest sessions.
- The GuestOS registry, session tracker, MIME types service and
  CrostiniManager now exist for guest profiles (redirected to the
  original profile), as the code paths above expect them. Borealis still
  has no service there: the Borealis publisher is only created when its
  service exists, and GuestOsRegistryService::GetEnabledApps() no longer
  assumes it (it also counts host apps as enabled, so they can handle
  links).
- GetGuestOsShelfAppId() matches a window's unprefixed app id to a host
  app's desktop file id or StartupWMClass, so windows group under the
  app's shelf item without sommelier.

